  "haplotype_notes": {
    "BCO1": "T alleles on BOTH rs12934922 AND rs7501331 = 69% reduced conversion. Combined poor converter frequency: ~10-15% European, ~5-8% East Asian, ~8-12% African",
    "GC": "Haplotypes: Gc1f (rs7041-T + rs4588-C), Gc1s (rs7041-G + rs4588-C), Gc2 (rs7041-T + rs4588-A). Gc2 associated with lowest VDBP levels. Gc1f highest in Africa (60-90%), Gc2 highest in Europe (25-30%)",
    "TAS2R38": "PAV haplotype (C-A-C) = supertaster; AVI haplotype (G-G-G) = non-taster. Strong LD (R2=0.80-0.90). PAV frequency: 49% EUR, 58% SAS, 66% EAS, 40% AFR. Rare haplotypes AAI (3-23%) and AAV (1-6%) more common in Africa"
  },
