  "methodology_notes": "Frequencies represent effect/risk allele percentages (0-100). Primary sources: gnomAD v4 (2024), 1000 Genomes Phase 3 (2015), ALFA database (2023), peer-reviewed population genetics studies. For gnomAD populations: NFE=Non-Finnish European, AFR=African/African American, AMR=Admixed American, EAS=East Asian, SAS=South Asian, MID=Middle Eastern. 1000G codes: YRI=Yoruba, LWK=Luhya, TSI=Tuscan, GBR=British, CHB=Han Chinese, JPT=Japanese. Where multiple studies available, ranges or averages reported. Admixed populations (gnomAD AFR, AMR) contain ancestry admixture affecting frequencies. TAS2R38 SNPs in strong linkage disequilibrium (LD), so individual SNP frequencies approximate PAV haplotype frequency."
